The sim bridge: a way in that does not pretend

Tandem now listens for the sim itself - ws://127.0.0.1:8796, on the frames it already speaks
for GSX - and ships the community package that talks to it. A profile names the simvars it
shares; anything not named is not read, not written, and not passed on. Off by default
(sim.enabled), so nothing changes until you say so.

Detection order is now: the sim's own answer, then GSX, then the flight files - and when none
of them can name an airframe that exists in the folder, it says exactly that instead of
picking a near miss. Livery and texture packages are out of the aircraft list: an A321 was
being read as "A320 EasyJet G-UZHN", a paint folder that won a match it had no business being
in. Install and remove are marker-based and refuse folders they did not create.
